ts on the  ground the ukrainians are doing pretty  well the russians are having big  logistical issues so the ukrainian  feeling is if they have that  safety from above and if the russians  are not allowed to bomb cities but also  ukrainian military then they have a much  better chance of  keeping their country  that's dw correspondent nick connolly in  kiev  well despite frequent shelling of  populated areas by russia u.s military  officials say there's been little change  on the ground over the past 24 hours but  one area where russian troops may be  making progress is in the city of  michilaiv which has seen heavy fighting  mikalev is key to russia's bid to seize  control of ukraine's black sea coast the  city of almost half a million is located  near the city of odessa which is  ukraine's main port mikalev has come  under heavy bombardment from russian  artillery  well joining me from mikkelav in ukraine  is the regional governor vitaly kim  thank you for speaking to us at this  very difficult time let me begin by  asking if the city of mikalai is still  under ukrainian control  yeah the city of megalife is still under  our control  and  also we  moved forward  to the gerson and sigirovka  in terms of the basics of food water  heating what are conditions like for  people in the city right now  about food medicine and water is okay in  the city in a big cities in our region  you know small  in small cities not small cities  small villages  there are some problems but we are  making our logistics to provide them all  they need there is no catastrophe but we  need  some storage because we have only one  way to supply for now  one road for supply for canal  and do you have a sense do you have  accurate updates  where exactly are the russian forces  right now in relation to your city  yes i have  all that data about this but i won't  won't tell you about it but because they  are moving  and  this is secret information i won't get  it  understood how likely is it that